SUMMARY:Free Edwards Summer Music Series: Latin Swing Orchestra
DESCRIPTION:Bass player Fhanor Molina began his musical training in Cali\, Colombia. He is a highly recognized Latin artist and founder of the Latin Swing Orchestra\, who carry forward the modern musical legacy of salsa and tropical music\, and tour throughout Ontario. \n\n\n\nThursday\, July 16\, 7 p.m.\n\n\n\nFree outdoor concert \n\n\n\nSee the rest of the Edwards Summer Music Series lineup here.  \n\n\n\nThis concert is part of the Edwards Summer Music Series\, which showcases diverse\, contemporary talent set within the natural beauty of the garden. Enjoy eight FREE outdoor concerts in the Garden on Thursday nights at 7 p.m. in July and August. General seating is available on a first-come basis. Guests can also bring their own chairs. Concerts are held rain or shine. \n\n\n\nThe Edwards Summer Music Series is generously supported by the Edwards Charitable Foundation and the presenting Sponsor Foresters Financial.
URL:https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/event/free-edwards-summer-music-series-latin-swing-orchestra/
LOCATION:ON
CATEGORIES:Edwards Summer Music Series
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/LATIN-SWING-ORCHESTRA.jpg
END:VEVENT
