SUMMARY:Free Edwards Summer Music Series: Mimi O’Bonsawin
DESCRIPTION:Mimi O’Bonsawin is an award-winning contemporary roots singer-songwriter from Northeastern Ontario and a member of the Odanak First Nation. Blending W8banaki (Abénaki) and French Canadian heritage with story-driven songwriting\, her music combines uplifting melodies\, acoustic instrumentation\, and a deep connection to the natural world. \n\n\n\nNamed Solo Artist of the Year at the 2025 Prix Trille Or Awards\, Mimi has toured across Canada\, Australia\, and France. Her acclaimed albums Willow\, Boréale\, and Live In Concert have earned national recognition and multiple award nominations. Performing as a duo with percussionist Ryan Schurman\, she creates intimate\, joyful\, and inspiring live performances. \n\n\n\nThursday\, July 23 at 7 p.m.\n\n\n\nFree outdoor concert \n\n\n\nSee the rest of the Edwards Summer Music Series lineup here. \n\n\n\nThis concert is part of the Edwards Summer Music Series\, which showcases diverse\, contemporary talent set within the natural beauty of the garden. Enjoy eight FREE outdoor concerts in the Garden on Thursday nights at 7 p.m. in July and August. General seating is available on a first-come basis. Guests can also bring their own chairs. Concerts are held rain or shine. \n\n\n\nThe Edwards Summer Music Series is generously supported by the Edwards Charitable Foundation and the presenting Sponsor Foresters Financial.
URL:https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/event/free-edwards-summer-music-series-mimi-obonsawin/
LOCATION:ON
CATEGORIES:Edwards Summer Music Series
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/MIMI-OBONSAWIN.jpg
END:VEVENT
