SUMMARY:Floral Design Program: Miniature\, Small\, and Large Floral Design
DESCRIPTION:Join us and learn about how to best utilize space in your designs!\nBy focusing on the size of various designs this course will illuminate questions of scale\, proportion\, and the use of space in design. The elements can be used surprisingly differently in different sizes of arrangements. Choosing plant material for your design can be challenging and creative mechanics may be needed to make it all work. But\, above all\, this course is fun!\n \nCourse fees do not include flowers or supplies. A materials list will be e-mailed prior to the start of each class.\n \nLearn more about our Certificate in Floral Design\n \nPrerequisites: Floral Design Fundamentals 1 & 2.\n \nTuesdays\, September 8\, 15\, 22\, & 29 from 6 to 9 p.m.\nPublic $240\, Members $190 (plus applicable taxes and fees)\n \nAbout Lil Taggart\nLil Taggart is an experienced and creative designer and instructor in Floral Arts. She is also an accredited Floral Design Judge and has competed on an international level as well as domestically. She serves on the board of Canada Blooms\, co-chairs the staging for the Toronto Flower Show\, is past president of the Georgetown Horticultural society and is a member of The Garden Club of Toronto.\n \nJoin Toronto Botanical Garden\nJoin the Toronto Botanical Garden (TBG) as a member to get a discount on this program\, upcoming events and classes\, and free parking. A TBG membership helps you deepen your knowledge and connection to the natural world\, become a part of a dynamic community of plant people\, and be inspired! Become a member!\n \nAdditional Program Information\n\n\n\nPlease review our Refund Policy and Terms of Agreement.\nFor more information on accessibility at the garden please review our Accessibility Features webpage. If you have any accessibility requirements during your program please email programsupport@torontobotnicalgarden.ca.\nTo learn more about the Toronto Botanical Garden and our programs\, please review our list of Frequently Asked Questions.
URL:https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/event/floral-design-program-miniature-small-and-large-floral-design-4/
